{
  "title": "Verb second: German word order",
  "note": "In a statement the conjugated verb is always the second element. If anything other than the subject comes first, the subject moves right after the verb: Heute gehe ich ins Kino. Question words also take the verb second; yes/no questions start with the verb. Und, aber, oder and denn don't count as a position.",
  "src": { "t": "Grimm Grammar: Wortstellung (word order)", "u": "https://coerll.utexas.edu/gg/gr/con_06.html" },
  "items": [
    { "c": "Heute ___ ins Kino.", "a": "gehe ich", "d": ["ich gehe"], "ex": "Heute gehe ich ins Kino.", "exT": "Today I'm going to the movies." },
    { "c": "Morgen ___ nach Hamburg.", "a": "fahren wir", "d": ["wir fahren"] },
    { "c": "Am Montag ___ Deutsch.", "a": "lerne ich", "d": ["ich lerne"] },
    { "c": "Leider ___ keine Zeit.", "a": "habe ich", "d": ["ich habe"], "ex": "Leider habe ich keine Zeit.", "exT": "Unfortunately I don't have time." },
    { "c": "Um acht Uhr ___.", "a": "kommt der Zug", "d": ["der Zug kommt"] },
    { "c": "In Berlin ___.", "a": "wohnt meine Tante", "d": ["meine Tante wohnt"] },
    { "c": "Dann ___ einen Kaffee.", "a": "trinken wir", "d": ["wir trinken"] },
    { "c": "Wo ___?", "a": "wohnst du", "d": ["du wohnst"], "ex": "Wo wohnst du?", "exT": "Where do you live?" },
    { "c": "Was ___ heute?", "a": "machst du", "d": ["du machst"] },
    { "c": "Ich bin müde, aber ___ noch.", "a": "ich arbeite", "d": ["arbeite ich"], "ex": "Ich bin müde, aber ich arbeite noch.", "exT": "I'm tired, but I'm still working." },
    { "c": "Er kommt nicht, denn ___ krank.", "a": "er ist", "d": ["ist er"] },
    { "c": "Ich trinke Tee und ___ Kaffee.", "a": "sie trinkt", "d": ["trinkt sie"] },
    { "c": "Am Wochenende ___ lange.", "a": "schlafen die Kinder", "d": ["die Kinder schlafen"] },
    { "c": "Morgen habe ich frei.", "a": "I'm off tomorrow.", "d": ["I was off yesterday.", "I'm busy tomorrow."] },
    { "c": "Kommst du mit?", "a": "Are you coming along?", "d": ["Are you coming later?", "Where are you coming from?"] },
    { "c": "Hast du Zeit?", "a": "Do you have time?", "d": ["What time is it?", "Do you have a watch?"] },
    { "c": "Spielst du Tennis?", "a": "Do you play tennis?", "d": ["Where do you play tennis?", "Let's play tennis!"] },
    { "c": "Ich spiele gern Tennis.", "a": "I like playing tennis.", "d": ["I play tennis often.", "I play tennis badly."], "ex": "Ich koche gern.", "exT": "I like to cook." },
    { "c": "gern", "a": "gladly, with pleasure", "d": ["often, usually", "badly, poorly"] },
    { "c": "dann", "a": "then", "d": ["there", "now"] },
    { "c": "leider", "a": "unfortunately", "d": ["luckily", "of course"] },
    { "c": "zuerst", "a": "first, at first", "d": ["finally", "afterward"] },
    { "c": "danach", "a": "afterward, after that", "d": ["before that", "at first"], "ex": "Zuerst esse ich, danach lerne ich.", "exT": "First I eat, then I study." },
    { "c": "hier", "a": "here", "d": ["there", "near"] },
    { "c": "dort", "a": "there", "d": ["here", "far away"] },
    { "c": "natürlich", "a": "of course, naturally", "d": ["unfortunately", "hardly"] },
    { "c": "Natürlich ___ dir.", "a": "helfe ich", "d": ["ich helfe"] },
    { "c": "Zuerst ___ Hausaufgaben.", "a": "mache ich", "d": ["ich mache"] }
  ],
  "read": {
    "title": "Ein Tag von Tim",
    "text": [
      "Tim ist Student in Köln. Am Morgen trinkt er einen Kaffee. Dann fährt er mit dem Bus zur Uni.",
      "Um neun Uhr hat er Mathe. Danach isst er ein Brötchen. Am Nachmittag arbeitet Tim in einem Café, aber er arbeitet nicht lange.",
      "Am Abend kocht er mit seiner Freundin Lea. Zuerst essen sie, dann lesen sie. Leider hat Tim morgen eine Prüfung. Heute geht er früh ins Bett."
    ],
    "q": [
      { "q": "How does Tim get to the university?", "o": ["On foot", "By car", "By bus"], "k": 2 },
      { "q": "What does Tim do after his math class?", "o": ["He drinks coffee", "He eats a roll", "He cooks"], "k": 1 },
      { "q": "Why does Tim go to bed early today?", "o": ["He has a test tomorrow", "He works early", "He is sick"], "k": 0 }
    ]
  }
}
